# Registration (spec 1.0). Pick the `dev` environment; read the mail at http://localhost:8025.
# With REGISTRATION_EMAIL_CONFIRMATION_ENABLED=false the first request answers 201 and you are done.
# Otherwise it answers 202 with an attemptId: copy it and the code (or the link's #token=…) from Mailpit.

### Register: 201 (active) or 202 (confirmation required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "someone+1@example.com",
  "password": "correct horse 1"
}

### Register the same email again: 409 email_taken
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "  Someone+1@Example.com ",
  "password": "another one 2"
}

### Confirm with the OTP from the email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attemptId": "<attemptId from the 202>",
  "code": "<6 digits from the email>"
}

### Confirm with a magic link (REGISTRATION_EMAIL_CONFIRMATION_METHOD=magic_link)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "<the value after #token= in the link>"
}

### Resend the email: 429 within 60 s of the last one, then 202
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "someone+1@example.com"
}

### A weak password: 400 validation_failed with the failing rules
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@example.com",
  "password": "short"
}
